Hi Azman,

To further Hugo's recommendation, you may find playing around with the mirt::itemplot(shiny=TRUE) interface useful for getting a feel for how/what the supported response models are capable of fitting and how this is reflected in the parameters (and in the classical parameterization transformations for unidimensional models). I generally recommend to those new to the package to get a feel for the IRT models that they are less familiar with first before trying to fit them in practice. HTH.

Phil

